er under the influence of negative emotions, like attachment and hatred.", "reference": "2018, Dalai Lama, translated by Dhondup Tsering, Introduction to Buddhism, →ISBN, page 8:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(countable) An entity that has such capacities.", "tags": ["countable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The great Intelligences fair\n That range above our mortal state,\n In circle round the blessed gate,\nReceived and gave him welcome there.", "reference": "1850, [Alfred, Lord Tennyson], “Canto LXXXIII”, in In Memoriam, London: Edward Moxon, […], →OCLC, page 118:"}, {"text": "The living intelligence, the Martian within the hood, was slain and splashed to the four winds of heaven, and the thing was now but a mere intricate device of metal whirling to destruction.", "reference": "1898, H.G. Wells, The War of the Worlds, London: Heinemann, page 102:"}, {"text": "But there are latent powers within man alone that are not yet fully understood and[…] we cannot definitely state what is, and what is not, due to the interference or influence of discarnate intelligences.", "reference": "1936, Rollo Ahmed, The Black Art, London: John Long Ltd, page 275:"}, {"text": "He passes beyond the projections and thought forms of his own creation to the wholly other and independent world of the angelic intelligences.", "reference": "1981, William Irwin Thompson, The Time Falling Bodies Take to Light: Mythology, Sexuality and the Origins of Culture, London: Rider/Hutchinson & Co., page 228:"}], "synonyms": ["intelligence", "sentient", "sapient", "sophont"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "intel·ligència"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "智能"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "inteligence"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "intelligens"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"},